@host = http://localhost:5080
@email = operador@example.com
@password = {{$processEnv BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD}}
@csrf = REPLACE_WITH_XSRF_TOKEN_COOKIE

### Obtain antiforgery cookies before login. Copy XSRF-TOKEN to csrf above.
GET {{host}}/auth/csrf

### The REST client must preserve both antiforgery cookies.
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{csrf}}

{"username": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}"}

### Current session
GET {{host}}/auth/me

### Refresh CSRF after login: the token is bound to the authenticated identity.
GET {{host}}/auth/csrf

### Accounts (requires the session cookie)
GET {{host}}/accounts

### Logout (update csrf with the authenticated token first)
POST {{host}}/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{csrf}}

{}
